What Is Information Security?
Information Security (Infosec) is all about protecting data from threats like unauthorized access, theft, damage, or attacks. This applies to how data is:
• 	Stored (e.g., on servers or devices)
• 	Transferred (e.g., over networks)
• 	Processed (e.g., by applications or systems)
To be considered secure, these systems must demonstrate specific properties—most importantly, the CIA Triad.

