🧾 Beyond CIA: Non-Repudiation
Another critical concept in secure systems is non-repudiation:
• 	It ensures that someone cannot deny having performed an action—like sending a message or signing a document.
• 	Example: A signed will with witnesses provides proof that the signer can't later deny having signed it.
This is vital for legal, financial, and communication systems where accountability matters.
